// Looks: themes, what each backend draws for a look (TESSERA.md decisions
// 6 and 7): glyphs for a terminal's map (text.tri) and for the watcher's
// window (tiles.tri).
//
// Cut points:
// - full, reduced, abstract, frozen: alike: how something looks to a
//            viewer has nothing to do with how it is simulated.
// - things:  a thing's look is its kind's (things.tri's #Look, declared
//            beside each kind); a terrain kind's, its own (terrain.tri).
// - code:    looks are resolved in src/looks.odin; `lab play` draws its map
//            in the text theme, the watcher its window in the tiles theme
//            (tessera/raylib's Theme matches a look by its name, then by the
//            part before its first dot, and draws a look it has nothing for
//            as its first letter). The view's own signs aren't looks: `@`
//            for oneself in `lab play`, water drawn over a tile.

package looks

// What a theme draws for a look, or a family of looks (the part of a look
// before its first dot): a glyph (`char`), in `ink`, on `ground` if it
// fills its tile (terrain), as red, green and blue, 0 to 255.
#Glyph: #Looks & { theme: "text" | "tiles", char: text, ink: [...int], ground: [...int] }
